      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "EL80uJy5rqSH2KVo11LX8",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785878070876,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Tokenization steps\n1. Splitting: \"inference engine\" → [\"inference\", \"engine\"] or subword tokens\n2. Vocabulary lookup: Each token maps to unique ID (vocab size ~50k–150k)\n3. Post-Processing: add special tokens, truncate to the context window\n4. Special tokens: Add <BOS>, <EOS>, and chat turn markers\n5. Batching: modern engines (vLLM) use ragged / continuous batching with\n    NO padding to a fixed length. Fixed-length padding is a training-era idea.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Tokenization steps\n1. Splitting: \"inference engine\" → [\"inference\", \"engine\"] or subword tokens\n2. Vocabulary lookup: Each token maps to unique ID (vocab size ~50k–150k)\n3. Post-Processing: add special tokens, truncate to the context window\n4. Special tokens: Add <BOS>, <EOS>, and chat turn markers\n5. Batching: modern engines (vLLM) use ragged / continuous batching with\n    NO padding to a fixed length. Fixed-length padding is a training-era idea.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "lONhs896vmnllF-4tVVYz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2254.3572261945847,
      "y": -1636.735721533152,
      "width": 549.6795043945312,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1574295422,
      "version": 677,
      "versionNonce": 1010364489,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "cF9k6KqMC3wASJJ_sJJQB",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785878070876,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "High-performance systems check an in-memory cache (like\na Hash Map) for frequently used words to bypass the\nalgorithmic splitting rules.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "High-performance systems check an in-memory cache (like\na Hash Map) for frequently used words to bypass the\nalgorithmic splitting rules.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "z8mkzJZEyx1bvwm_hQCYi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2254.3572261945847,
      "y": -1296.7570520098784,
      "width": 486.95947265625,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 314129022,
      "version": 671,
      "versionNonce": 1766732297,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "fbp91Ie1oM-Jb-sM9EIyk",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785878070876,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The subword fragments are matched against a\nstatic, pre-trained dictionary (the vocab.json file)\nto find their unique numerical IDs.\n\nExample: you type the fictional word \"Zorblax\".\n\nBPE works BOTTOM-UP, not top-down. It does\nNOT look up the\nwhole word and then split it on failure.\nIt starts from raw bytes/characters and\nMERGES upward using\na ranked merge table (merges.txt):\n  Z,o,r,b,l,a,x  ->  Zor,bl,ax  ->  Zorb,lax\nAt each pass it applies the highest-priority merge\nrule still\navailable, stopping when none match.\n\n(Top-down greedy longest-match splitting is\nWordPiece/BERT,\na different algorithm.)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The subword fragments are matched against a static, pre-trained dictionary (the vocab.json file) to find their unique numerical IDs.\n\nExample: you type the fictional word \"Zorblax\".\n\nBPE works BOTTOM-UP, not top-down. It does NOT look up the\nwhole word and then split it on failure.\nIt starts from raw bytes/characters and MERGES upward using\na ranked merge table (merges.txt):\n  Z,o,r,b,l,a,x  ->  Zor,bl,ax  ->  Zorb,lax\nAt each pass it applies the highest-priority merge rule still\navailable, stopping when none match.\n\n(Top-down greedy longest-match splitting is WordPiece/BERT,\na different algorithm.)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aftmdgP4wzkLakdar8zuw",
