    {
      "id": "ogAg3MtzayWhQBMFfhqV-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2254.3572261945847,
      "y": -732.7870291116749,
      "width": 756,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1295637438,
      "version": 515,
      "versionNonce": 1045718409,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "YVrQnv6cmQ9Jx7nBrLxUZ",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785878070876,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What if you type a character that isn't even in the alphabet\nof the vocabulary?\n\nFor byte-level BPE (GPT-2/3/4, tiktoken) this NEVER happens.\nThe 256 raw byte values ARE the base of the vocabulary, so\nevery possible input is representable by construction.\nThere is no <UNK> token at all, ever.\n\n\"Byte fallback\" as a distinct named feature belongs to\nSentencePiece / Llama-style tokenizers, which start from\ncharacters and drop to raw bytes only for unseen ones.\n\n* Either way the unknown character becomes a sequence of\nbase byte tokens, and the vocab reserves 256 slots (0x00-0xFF).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What if you type a character that isn't even in the alphabet\nof the vocabulary?\n\nFor byte-level BPE (GPT-2/3/4, tiktoken) this NEVER happens.\nThe 256 raw byte values ARE the base of the vocabulary, so\nevery possible input is representable by construction.\nThere is no <UNK> token at all, ever.\n\n\"Byte fallback\" as a distinct named feature belongs to\nSentencePiece / Llama-style tokenizers, which start from\ncharacters and drop to raw bytes only for unseen ones.\n\n* Either way the unknown character becomes a sequence of\nbase byte tokens, and the vocab reserves 256 slots (0x00-0xFF).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
