      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1667389423,
      "version": 1077,
      "versionNonce": 13185639,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "430bJPHugnEzWfsYM32p1",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785878054870,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Queries_Q = [\n    [ 0.5774, -0.4181,  1.3440,  0.9158 ],  # Token 0 Query Vector\n    [ 1.4875, -0.7328, -0.5561,  1.3783 ],  # Token 1 Query Vector\n    [ 0.8298, -0.5705,  0.6385,  0.5965 ]   # Token 2 Query Vector\n]\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Queries_Q = [\n    [ 0.5774, -0.4181,  1.3440,  0.9158 ],  # Token 0 Query Vector\n    [ 1.4875, -0.7328, -0.5561,  1.3783 ],  # Token 1 Query Vector\n    [ 0.8298, -0.5705,  0.6385,  0.5965 ]   # Token 2 Query Vector\n]\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jCOHna0WNtqZlPRfOeTnL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2963.226909811039,
      "y": 3409.9898113615736,
      "width": 775.4592895507812,
      "height": 975,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 748941473,
      "version": 1519,
      "versionNonce": 187630759,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "-XE0pkIZLYW7-FWc6pK5z",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785878054871,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The transformation happens by multiplying your 3 X 4 input matrix against \nthree distinct, pre-trained weight matrices (W_q, W_k, W_v) stored in the \nmodel's parameters.\n\n1. The Pre-Trained Weights (Stored in VRAM)\nBecause your tokens have a hidden dimension size of 4, each \nprojection weight matrix must be a (4 X 4) square matrix to \nmap the 4 input values to 4 output values.\n\nLet's look closely at how the Query Projection Matrix (W_q) \nprocesses your data using these example weight values:\n\nW_q=  0.5 -0.2  0.1   0.8\n        -0.1  0.6  0.3  -0.4\n        0.2  0.1   0.9  0.2\n        0.7  -0.5 -0.3  0.6\n\n2. The Mathematical Transformation (Row by Row)\nThe GPU's Tensor Cores calculate the dot product of every token \nrow against every column of the weight matrix. Here is how Token 0 \ntransitions into its new Query vector:\n\nToken 0 Input Row= (0.2389 -0.8959 1.7720 0.0199 )\n\nOutput Dimension 1: (0.2389 X 0.5) + (-0.8959 X -0.1) + (1.7720 X 0.2) + \n                         (0.0199 X 0.7) = 0.5774\nOutput Dimension 2: (0.2389 X -0.2) + (-0.8959 X 0.6) + (1.7720 X 0.1) + \n                         (0.0199 X -0.5) = -0.4181\nOutput Dimension 3: (0.2389 X 0.1) + (-0.8959 X 0.3) + (1.7720 X 0.9) + \n                         (0.0199 X -0.3) = 1.3440\nOutput Dimension 4: (0.2389 X 0.8) + (-0.8959 X -0.4) + (1.7720 X 0.2) + \n                         (0.0199 X 0.6) = 0.9158\n3. The Final Output Matrices\nThe exact same row-by-column operation runs simultaneously for all 3 tokens\nacross three separate weight tables. The final result creates three completely \nindependent matrix structures ready for attention:\n\nThe Query Matrix (Q = X * W_q)\nEach row is now asking its unique structural question to the rest of the text.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The transformation happens by multiplying your 3 X 4 input matrix against \nthree distinct, pre-trained weight matrices (W_q, W_k, W_v) stored in the \nmodel's parameters.\n\n1. The Pre-Trained Weights (Stored in VRAM)\nBecause your tokens have a hidden dimension size of 4, each \nprojection weight matrix must be a (4 X 4) square matrix to \nmap the 4 input values to 4 output values.\n\nLet's look closely at how the Query Projection Matrix (W_q) \nprocesses your data using these example weight values:\n\nW_q=  0.5 -0.2  0.1   0.8\n        -0.1  0.6  0.3  -0.4\n        0.2  0.1   0.9  0.2\n        0.7  -0.5 -0.3  0.6\n\n2. The Mathematical Transformation (Row by Row)\nThe GPU's Tensor Cores calculate the dot product of every token \nrow against every column of the weight matrix. Here is how Token 0 \ntransitions into its new Query vector:\n\nToken 0 Input Row= (0.2389 -0.8959 1.7720 0.0199 )\n\nOutput Dimension 1: (0.2389 X 0.5) + (-0.8959 X -0.1) + (1.7720 X 0.2) + \n                         (0.0199 X 0.7) = 0.5774\nOutput Dimension 2: (0.2389 X -0.2) + (-0.8959 X 0.6) + (1.7720 X 0.1) + \n                         (0.0199 X -0.5) = -0.4181\nOutput Dimension 3: (0.2389 X 0.1) + (-0.8959 X 0.3) + (1.7720 X 0.9) + \n                         (0.0199 X -0.3) = 1.3440\nOutput Dimension 4: (0.2389 X 0.8) + (-0.8959 X -0.4) + (1.7720 X 0.2) + \n                         (0.0199 X 0.6) = 0.9158\n3. The Final Output Matrices\nThe exact same row-by-column operation runs simultaneously for all 3 tokens\nacross three separate weight tables. The final result creates three completely \nindependent matrix structures ready for attention:\n\nThe Query Matrix (Q = X * W_q)\nEach row is now asking its unique structural question to the rest of the text.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
