      "index": "b4D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1142483023,
      "version": 1453,
      "versionNonce": 800140984,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "Il3Nwg50bYK7HgI97cjyR",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785876468302,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. The Stabilizer: Scaling (sqrt{d_k})\nDivide every score by the square root of the HEAD dimension\n(not the full hidden size) - here sqrt{4} = 2, but sqrt{128}\nin a real Llama 3 head. This keeps dot-product variance near\n1.0 so Softmax cannot saturate into a near one-hot spike.\nNOTE: at inference there are no gradients. Softmax saturation\nis the real reason; gradient stability is a training benefit.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. The Stabilizer: Scaling (sqrt{d_k})\nDivide every score by the square root of the HEAD dimension\n(not the full hidden size) - here sqrt{4} = 2, but sqrt{128}\nin a real Llama 3 head. This keeps dot-product variance near\n1.0 so Softmax cannot saturate into a near one-hot spike.\nNOTE: at inference there are no gradients. Softmax saturation\nis the real reason; gradient stability is a training benefit.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
