    {
      "id": "BkYVgYr3Nfx2Xno9Ttaie",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3546.2071501204173,
      "y": 10378.707804477534,
      "width": 927.3183265265716,
      "height": 1325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1619863518,
      "version": 1700,
      "versionNonce": 1442435207,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "bumf5-VFrQzkqRiXxVOqp",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785878120746,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "    The Up Path weight matrix (W_up) acts as a massive repository of the model's factual\nknowledge, reasoning rules, and vocabulary associations.\n\n    While the Attention block calculates how words relate to each other, the (W_up) matrix is\nwhere the model actually \"thinks\" about the concept itself. It extracts complex hidden\nattributes from your prompt vectors and blows them up into an expanded mathematical\nworkspace.\n\n    Here is the exact breakdown of what this weight matrix is and its precise dimensions using\nyour [1000 x 4096] example.\n\n1. The Dimensions of W_up\n    To transform your prompt matrix from 4,096 columns to 14,336 columns, the W_up matrix\nmust have the following shape: Shape of W_up= [4096 x 14336]\n\nWhen your prompt hits this matrix on the GPU, the linear algebra looks like this:\n    [Prompt Matrix] X [Up Weight Matrix] --> [Up Path Output]\n    \n    [1000 x 4096] x [4096 x 14336] --> [1000 x 14336]\n\n2. What actually is this weight matrix?\n    The W_up matrix consists of 58,720,256 individual floating-point numbers (parameters)\nstored in the GPU's VRAM for a single layer.\n\n    During the pre-training phase (when the model read trillions of words from the internet),\nthese 58 million numbers were slowly adjusted. You can think of each of the 14,336 columns as\na highly specialized \"concept detector\" or \"knowledge slot\":\n\n    - Slot 42 might activate heavily if a token represents a programming language syntax error.\n    - Slot 1,029 might activate if a token represents a medical symptom related to cardiology.\n    - Slot 12,440 might activate if the text shifts to a formal, academic writing tone.\n\n3. How the Up Path brings data about your prompt\n    When your [1000 x 4096] prompt matrix multiplies against W_up, it triggers an explosion\nof semantic cross-references for every single one of your 1,000 tokens:\n\n    1. The Vector Interaction: The GPU's Tensor Cores map your 4,096 context numbers\nacross all 14,336 specialized columns.\n    2. Feature Extraction: If Token #500 in your prompt is the word \"Apple\", its 4,096\nnumbers will mathematically align with the specific columns in W_up that hold information about\ntechnology corporations, orchard farming, fruit anatomy, and cellular biology.\n    3. The Raw Brain Dump: The output [1000 x 14336] matrix becomes a massive, unfiltered\n\"brain dump\" containing every piece of encyclopedic information the model knows about those\nwords in parallel.\n\nWhy it needs to be so wide (14,336)\n    Human language and knowledge are incredibly high-dimensional. If you tried to pack all the\nfactual concepts of the universe into just 4,096 dimensions, the concepts would crowd each\nother out, and the model would get confused.\n    By expanding the matrix to 14,336 columns, the model creates a wide-open playing field.\nThis space allows it to disentangle complex concepts, separating \"Apple the phone\" from \"Apple\nthe pie fruit\" cleanly, before the Gate Path cuts away the irrelevant thoughts in the next\nstep.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "    The Up Path weight matrix (W_up) acts as a massive repository of the model's factual knowledge, reasoning rules, and vocabulary associations.\n\n    While the Attention block calculates how words relate to each other, the (W_up) matrix is where the model actually \"thinks\" about the concept itself. It extracts complex hidden attributes from your prompt vectors and blows them up into an expanded mathematical workspace.\n\n    Here is the exact breakdown of what this weight matrix is and its precise dimensions using your [1000 x 4096] example.\n\n1. The Dimensions of W_up\n    To transform your prompt matrix from 4,096 columns to 14,336 columns, the W_up matrix must have the following shape: Shape of W_up= [4096 x 14336]\n\nWhen your prompt hits this matrix on the GPU, the linear algebra looks like this:\n    [Prompt Matrix] X [Up Weight Matrix] --> [Up Path Output]\n    \n    [1000 x 4096] x [4096 x 14336] --> [1000 x 14336]\n\n2. What actually is this weight matrix?\n    The W_up matrix consists of 58,720,256 individual floating-point numbers (parameters) stored in the GPU's VRAM for a single layer.\n\n    During the pre-training phase (when the model read trillions of words from the internet), these 58 million numbers were slowly adjusted. You can think of each of the 14,336 columns as a highly specialized \"concept detector\" or \"knowledge slot\":\n\n    - Slot 42 might activate heavily if a token represents a programming language syntax error.\n    - Slot 1,029 might activate if a token represents a medical symptom related to cardiology.\n    - Slot 12,440 might activate if the text shifts to a formal, academic writing tone.\n\n3. How the Up Path brings data about your prompt\n    When your [1000 x 4096] prompt matrix multiplies against W_up, it triggers an explosion of semantic cross-references for every single one of your 1,000 tokens:\n\n    1. The Vector Interaction: The GPU's Tensor Cores map your 4,096 context numbers across all 14,336 specialized columns.\n    2. Feature Extraction: If Token #500 in your prompt is the word \"Apple\", its 4,096 numbers will mathematically align with the specific columns in W_up that hold information about technology corporations, orchard farming, fruit anatomy, and cellular biology.\n    3. The Raw Brain Dump: The output [1000 x 14336] matrix becomes a massive, unfiltered \"brain dump\" containing every piece of encyclopedic information the model knows about those words in parallel.\n\nWhy it needs to be so wide (14,336)\n    Human language and knowledge are incredibly high-dimensional. If you tried to pack all the factual concepts of the universe into just 4,096 dimensions, the concepts would crowd each other out, and the model would get confused.\n    By expanding the matrix to 14,336 columns, the model creates a wide-open playing field. This space allows it to disentangle complex concepts, separating \"Apple the phone\" from \"Apple the pie fruit\" cleanly, before the Gate Path cuts away the irrelevant thoughts in the next step.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
