    {
      "id": "Qo2z7xonIBWOAQo9kNaU_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3709.8366280357086,
      "y": 9888.252686271728,
      "width": 952.3514537975277,
      "height": 1125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 777313666,
      "version": 1485,
      "versionNonce": 606622904,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "5h8I5ZgrD00jI0ZD7detV",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "3GwMhFlX2FERydeYQowAV",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785876703018,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Gate Path weight matrix W_gate acts as the model's dynamic cognitive router.\n\n    While the Up Path W_up performs a massive, unfiltered \"brain dump\" of every possible idea\nrelated to your tokens, the Gate Path has the exact opposite job. It analyzes the context of\nyour prompt and creates a precise, element-by-element matching mask to block irrelevant data\nand let the correct logic pass through.\n\n1. The Dimensions of W_gate\n    To match the expanded workspace of the Up Path, the W_gate matrix uses the exact same\nfootprint:\n    Shape of W_gate = [4096 x 14336] \nWhen your prompt hits this matrix on the GPU, the linear algebra mirrors its sibling:\n    [Prompt Matrix] x [Gate Weight Matrix] --> [Gate Path Output]\n    [1000 x 4096] x [4096 x 14336] --> [1000 x 14336]\n\n2. What actually is this weight matrix?\n    Like W_up, the W_gate matrix consists of 58,720,256 individual parameters frozen in VRAM.\n    However, during training, its numbers were optimized to recognize contextual conditions rather\nthan pure facts. You can think of each of the 14,336 columns in W_gate as a \"relevance dimmer\nswitch\" that perfectly aligns with the knowledge slots in W_up:\n    - Switch 42 (Programming): Turns ON if surrounding tokens look like code. It turns OFF if\nthe text is a cooking recipe.\n    - Switch 1,029 (Cardiology): Turns ON if words like \"heart\", \"pulse\", or \"chest\" are nearby.\n    - Switch 12,440 (Academic Tone): Turns ON if the user asked for a research paper summary.\n\n3. How the Gate Path filters data about your prompt\n    When your [1000 x 4096] prompt matrix multiplies against W_gate, it calculates a customized\nfiltering profile for all 1,000 tokens:\n    - Contextual Evaluation: The GPU maps your tokens across all 14,336 condition switches.\n    - The Smooth Activation (SiLU): The raw output numbers are immediately pushed through the\nSiLU (Swish) function. This mathematically squashes every value into a clean percentage between\n0.0 (Full Block) and 1.0 (Full Pass).\n    - The Target Application: If Token #500 is \"Apple\" and your prompt is \"Apple stock price\ntoday\", the Gate Path calculates a 1.0 for columns tracking finance and corporate data, and a\n0.0 for columns tracking fruit farming or baking recipes.\n\nWhy it needs to be so wide (14,336)\n    The filter matrix must be exactly as wide as the idea matrix so they can collide perfectly in\nthe next step.\n\n    Because human language relies entirely on context, a fact in W_up is completely useless\nwithout an equally nuanced filter in W_gate to regulate it. By providing 14,336 distinct dimmer\nswitches, the model ensures that when the two paths are multiplied element-wise SiLU(Gate)}\nodot Up), the irrelevant meanings of ambiguous words are instantly erased, leaving only the clean,\ncontext-correct logic to move forward.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Gate Path weight matrix W_gate acts as the model's dynamic cognitive router.\n\n    While the Up Path W_up performs a massive, unfiltered \"brain dump\" of every possible idea related to your tokens, the Gate Path has the exact opposite job. It analyzes the context of your prompt and creates a precise, element-by-element matching mask to block irrelevant data and let the correct logic pass through.\n\n1. The Dimensions of W_gate\n    To match the expanded workspace of the Up Path, the W_gate matrix uses the exact same footprint:\n    Shape of W_gate = [4096 x 14336] \nWhen your prompt hits this matrix on the GPU, the linear algebra mirrors its sibling:\n    [Prompt Matrix] x [Gate Weight Matrix] --> [Gate Path Output]\n    [1000 x 4096] x [4096 x 14336] --> [1000 x 14336]\n\n2. What actually is this weight matrix?\n    Like W_up, the W_gate matrix consists of 58,720,256 individual parameters frozen in VRAM.\n    However, during training, its numbers were optimized to recognize contextual conditions rather than pure facts. You can think of each of the 14,336 columns in W_gate as a \"relevance dimmer switch\" that perfectly aligns with the knowledge slots in W_up:\n    - Switch 42 (Programming): Turns ON if surrounding tokens look like code. It turns OFF if the text is a cooking recipe.\n    - Switch 1,029 (Cardiology): Turns ON if words like \"heart\", \"pulse\", or \"chest\" are nearby.\n    - Switch 12,440 (Academic Tone): Turns ON if the user asked for a research paper summary.\n\n3. How the Gate Path filters data about your prompt\n    When your [1000 x 4096] prompt matrix multiplies against W_gate, it calculates a customized filtering profile for all 1,000 tokens:\n    - Contextual Evaluation: The GPU maps your tokens across all 14,336 condition switches.\n    - The Smooth Activation (SiLU): The raw output numbers are immediately pushed through the SiLU (Swish) function. This mathematically squashes every value into a clean percentage between 0.0 (Full Block) and 1.0 (Full Pass).\n    - The Target Application: If Token #500 is \"Apple\" and your prompt is \"Apple stock price today\", the Gate Path calculates a 1.0 for columns tracking finance and corporate data, and a 0.0 for columns tracking fruit farming or baking recipes.\n\nWhy it needs to be so wide (14,336)\n    The filter matrix must be exactly as wide as the idea matrix so they can collide perfectly in the next step.\n\n    Because human language relies entirely on context, a fact in W_up is completely useless without an equally nuanced filter in W_gate to regulate it. By providing 14,336 distinct dimmer switches, the model ensures that when the two paths are multiplied element-wise SiLU(Gate)} odot Up), the irrelevant meanings of ambiguous words are instantly erased, leaving only the clean, context-correct logic to move forward.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
