      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# LLM Inference Pipeline: LM Head Layer Deep Dive\n\n## 0. Input Layer Egress\n* **Data Source:** Standalone Post-Transformer RMSNorm Layer.\n* **Matrix Shape:** `[Sequence Length x Hidden Dimension]` $\\rightarrow$\n`[1000 x 4096]`.\n* **State:** Every element is numerically stabilized, variance-scaled to\n1.0, and contextually optimized across all hidden channels.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Vocabulary Projection (The LM Head MatMul)\nThe `[1000 x 4096]` dense matrix hits a massive linear layer known as the\n**LM Head** (Language Model Head). This operation functions as the exact\nmathematical inverse of the Token Embedding step found at the absolute\nbeginning of the LLM.\n\n### Mathematical Formula\n$$\\text{Logits} = X_{\\text{normed}} \\times W_{\\text{lm\\_head}}$$\n\n* **$X_{\\text{normed}}$ (Input):** The normalized token matrix `[1000 x\n4096]`.\n* **$W_{\\text{lm\\_head}}$ (Weights):** The dictionary mapping matrix of\nshape `[4096 x Vocabulary Size]`. For a standard Llama 3 architecture, the\nvocabulary footprint is exactly `128,256`.\n\n### Linear Algebra Profile\n$$\\text{[1000 x 4096]} \\times \\text{[4096 x 128,256]} \\longrightarrow\n\\mathbf{[1000 x 128,256]}$$\n\n### Execution Profile\n* **Hardware:** This step is highly compute-bound. The GPU floods its\nhigh-speed **Tensor Cores** across a 525M-parameter weight matrix\n(4096 x 128,256). NOTE: 525M is the PARAMETER COUNT, not a per-cycle\nrate - the matmul takes many thousands of cycles, tiled across the SMs.\n* **Output:** A 2D matrix of **Raw Scores (Logits)**. For each of your\n1,000 prompt tokens, the model has now spit out a raw numeric score for\nall 128,256 possible words in its dictionary.\n\n---\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# LLM Inference Pipeline: LM Head Layer Deep Dive\n\n## 0. Input Layer Egress\n* **Data Source:** Standalone Post-Transformer RMSNorm Layer.\n* **Matrix Shape:** `[Sequence Length x Hidden Dimension]` $\\rightarrow$\n`[1000 x 4096]`.\n* **State:** Every element is numerically stabilized, variance-scaled to\n1.0, and contextually optimized across all hidden channels.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Vocabulary Projection (The LM Head MatMul)\nThe `[1000 x 4096]` dense matrix hits a massive linear layer known as the\n**LM Head** (Language Model Head). This operation functions as the exact\nmathematical inverse of the Token Embedding step found at the absolute\nbeginning of the LLM.\n\n### Mathematical Formula\n$$\\text{Logits} = X_{\\text{normed}} \\times W_{\\text{lm\\_head}}$$\n\n* **$X_{\\text{normed}}$ (Input):** The normalized token matrix `[1000 x\n4096]`.\n* **$W_{\\text{lm\\_head}}$ (Weights):** The dictionary mapping matrix of\nshape `[4096 x Vocabulary Size]`. For a standard Llama 3 architecture, the\nvocabulary footprint is exactly `128,256`.\n\n### Linear Algebra Profile\n$$\\text{[1000 x 4096]} \\times \\text{[4096 x 128,256]} \\longrightarrow\n\\mathbf{[1000 x 128,256]}$$\n\n### Execution Profile\n* **Hardware:** This step is highly compute-bound. The GPU floods its\nhigh-speed **Tensor Cores** across a 525M-parameter weight matrix\n(4096 x 128,256). NOTE: 525M is the PARAMETER COUNT, not a per-cycle\nrate - the matmul takes many thousands of cycles, tiled across the SMs.\n* **Output:** A 2D matrix of **Raw Scores (Logits)**. For each of your\n1,000 prompt tokens, the model has now spit out a raw numeric score for\nall 128,256 possible words in its dictionary.\n\n---\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "q6UVLpa4o1_tgxTzpoHe0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2251.1373501089765,
      "y": 16371.948134779606,
      "width": 1124.501074204721,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
