          "id": "dFbuCjZFYlGzz5JIlMf7R",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785876389333,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n## Step 3: Probability Distribution Calculation (Softmax)\nThe 128,256 unscaled, chaotic numbers in that final row vector must be converted into clean, usable\nprobabilities. The vector is routed into the final **Softmax activation function**.\n\n### Mathematical Formula\n$$\\text{Probability}(w_i) = \\frac{e^{\\text{Logits}_i}}{\\sum_{j=1}^{V} e^{\\text{Logits}_j}}$$\n\n* **Where $V$:** The total vocabulary size (`128,256`).\n\n### Execution Profile\n* **The Elimination:** The exponent base $e$ forces all raw numbers (even large negative ones) into\nstrictly positive numbers. \n* **The Normalization:** The sum ($\\sum$) ensures that when every vocabulary slot is divided by the grand\ntotal, they form clean percentages between `0.0` and `1.0` that sum up to **exactly 100%**.\n* **Output:** A clean 1D percentage array over the dictionary (e.g., `\"the\"` = 62.4%, `\"water\"` = 21.1%,\n`\"code\"` = 0.003%).\n\n---",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n## Step 3: Probability Distribution Calculation (Softmax)\nThe 128,256 unscaled, chaotic numbers in that final row vector must be converted into clean, usable probabilities. The vector is routed into the final **Softmax activation function**.\n\n### Mathematical Formula\n$$\\text{Probability}(w_i) = \\frac{e^{\\text{Logits}_i}}{\\sum_{j=1}^{V} e^{\\text{Logits}_j}}$$\n\n* **Where $V$:** The total vocabulary size (`128,256`).\n\n### Execution Profile\n* **The Elimination:** The exponent base $e$ forces all raw numbers (even large negative ones) into strictly positive numbers. \n* **The Normalization:** The sum ($\\sum$) ensures that when every vocabulary slot is divided by the grand total, they form clean percentages between `0.0` and `1.0` that sum up to **exactly 100%**.\n* **Output:** A clean 1D percentage array over the dictionary (e.g., `\"the\"` = 62.4%, `\"water\"` = 21.1%, `\"code\"` = 0.003%).\n\n---",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "csQ7pn-xQZTJ4jLDZEcwf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2251.1373501089765,
      "y": 17995.75129433898,
      "width": 1368.2079747057428,
      "height": 168,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1916860009,
      "version": 643,
      "versionNonce": 2028213176,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "pcgp_fLD9rQjw4njIYNaS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785876369440,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## 4. Next Destination: The Token Selector (Sampling / Argmax)\n* **Final Product:** A 1D probability array of shape **`[128,256]`**.\n* **Next Component:** The **Selection Engine**. If `temperature = 0`, it triggers an **Argmax** function to\ninstantly extract the index of the highest percentage token. If temperature > 0, it applies **Top-P / Top-K sampling\nmechanics** to pick the next token. \n* **The Exit:** The chosen single integer ID (e.g., `1240`) leaves the GPU hardware and heads to the CPU\n**Detokenizer** to be translated into human text and printed on the screen.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## 4. Next Destination: The Token Selector (Sampling / Argmax)\n* **Final Product:** A 1D probability array of shape **`[128,256]`**.\n* **Next Component:** The **Selection Engine**. If `temperature = 0`, it triggers an **Argmax** function to instantly extract the index of the highest percentage token. If temperature > 0, it applies **Top-P / Top-K sampling mechanics** to pick the next token. \n* **The Exit:** The chosen single integer ID (e.g., `1240`) leaves the GPU hardware and heads to the CPU **Detokenizer** to be translated into human text and printed on the screen.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
