      "updated": 1785876650994,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. The EOS Token is Natively in the Vocabulary Table\nInside the model's vocabulary list, alongside thousands of human words, there are unique control codes:\n    - Llama 3 has TWO distinct stop tokens: 128001 = <|end_of_text|> and\n      128009 = <|eot_id|> (end of a chat turn). They are different IDs,\n      and a chat server must treat BOTH as terminal.\n\nDuring the model's training phase, it read billions of complete web pages and articles. Every time an \narticle ended, a human trainer or data pipeline appended that special closing token to the end of the text. \n\nAs a result, the model's internal weights learned a very strong rule: when a thought or answer is logically \ncomplete, give slot 128001 a massive score.\n\n\n2. The Moment of Termination (How it works in the loop)\nLet's look at what happens in the selection engine during the loop, say at Token #1045:\n\n    - The LM Head Output: The model projects your vector out to the 128,256 row.\n    - The Softmax Probability: The attention history and the FFN blocks determine that the answer is perfectly finished. \n      The Softmax function outputs these percentages:\n        - \" because\" = 0.01%\n        - \" water\" = 0.002%\n        - <|eot_id|> (Slot 128001) = 98.5%\n\nThe Selection Engine: The Argmax or Sampling algorithm rolls the dice or selects the maximum value. It picks the integer ID: 128001.\n\n3. Closing the Door on the CPU\nThe single integer 128001 splits and travels down our parallel tracks just like any other word, but the behavior changes:\n\n    - On the GPU Track: The loop code has a hardcoded conditional safety check wrapper. The wrapper states: if selected_id == eos_token_id: break. \nThe loop instantly terminates. The GPU clears the active registers, freezes further forward passes, and stops processing.\n\n    - On the CPU Detokenizer Track: The Detokenizer receives 128001. It checks tokenizer.json, sees that it is a special system \nformatting string, and completely hides it from the user. It prints nothing to stdout.\n\n\n4. The Safety Net: Hard Token Limits\nWhat if the model gets confused and keeps generating text without ever outputting the <|eot_id|> token?\n\nTo protect the server hardware, inference engines (like Hugging Face, vLLM, or OpenAI's API) force you to specify a Hard Safety \nNet Limit via parameters such as max_new_tokens = 512 or max_tokens.\n\nThe execution engine runs a manual counter on the CPU during the loop:\n\ntoken_count = 0\nwhile True:\n    # ... GPU calculates token ...\n    token_count += 1\n    if token_id == EOS_TOKEN or token_count >= max_new_tokens:\n        break # Hard stop\n\n\nIf the model hits your designated threshold (e.g., it generates 512 words without stopping naturally), the CPU forcefully breaks the loop, \nshuts down the forward passes, and returns the text generated up to that exact cutoff marker.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. The EOS Token is Natively in the Vocabulary Table\nInside the model's vocabulary list, alongside thousands of human words, there are unique control codes:\n    - Llama 3 has TWO distinct stop tokens: 128001 = <|end_of_text|> and\n      128009 = <|eot_id|> (end of a chat turn). They are different IDs,\n      and a chat server must treat BOTH as terminal.\n\nDuring the model's training phase, it read billions of complete web pages and articles. Every time an \narticle ended, a human trainer or data pipeline appended that special closing token to the end of the text. \n\nAs a result, the model's internal weights learned a very strong rule: when a thought or answer is logically \ncomplete, give slot 128001 a massive score.\n\n\n2. The Moment of Termination (How it works in the loop)\nLet's look at what happens in the selection engine during the loop, say at Token #1045:\n\n    - The LM Head Output: The model projects your vector out to the 128,256 row.\n    - The Softmax Probability: The attention history and the FFN blocks determine that the answer is perfectly finished. \n      The Softmax function outputs these percentages:\n        - \" because\" = 0.01%\n        - \" water\" = 0.002%\n        - <|eot_id|> (Slot 128001) = 98.5%\n\nThe Selection Engine: The Argmax or Sampling algorithm rolls the dice or selects the maximum value. It picks the integer ID: 128001.\n\n3. Closing the Door on the CPU\nThe single integer 128001 splits and travels down our parallel tracks just like any other word, but the behavior changes:\n\n    - On the GPU Track: The loop code has a hardcoded conditional safety check wrapper. The wrapper states: if selected_id == eos_token_id: break. \nThe loop instantly terminates. The GPU clears the active registers, freezes further forward passes, and stops processing.\n\n    - On the CPU Detokenizer Track: The Detokenizer receives 128001. It checks tokenizer.json, sees that it is a special system \nformatting string, and completely hides it from the user. It prints nothing to stdout.\n\n\n4. The Safety Net: Hard Token Limits\nWhat if the model gets confused and keeps generating text without ever outputting the <|eot_id|> token?\n\nTo protect the server hardware, inference engines (like Hugging Face, vLLM, or OpenAI's API) force you to specify a Hard Safety \nNet Limit via parameters such as max_new_tokens = 512 or max_tokens.\n\nThe execution engine runs a manual counter on the CPU during the loop:\n\ntoken_count = 0\nwhile True:\n    # ... GPU calculates token ...\n    token_count += 1\n    if token_id == EOS_TOKEN or token_count >= max_new_tokens:\n        break # Hard stop\n\n\nIf the model hits your designated threshold (e.g., it generates 512 words without stopping naturally), the CPU forcefully breaks the loop, \nshuts down the forward passes, and returns the text generated up to that exact cutoff marker.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "softmax-deepdive-restored",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -8202.073233045918,
      "y": 8184.212223023439,
      "width": 783.0237387249863,
      "height": 1280.3,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#0d9488",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1427958287,
      "version": 1724,
      "versionNonce": 1105189560,
